#: ../../modules/core/core_terms_maps_comparisons.rst:172
msgid ":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Abs` for absolute value"
msgstr ":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Abs` para el valor absoluto"

#: ../../modules/core/core_terms_maps_comparisons.rst:174
msgid ""
"``Abs`` is the one function with no derivative: it is not differentiable "
"at zero and there is no ``sign`` node to write its derivative with, so "
":meth:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Expression.diff` raises on it."
msgstr ""
"``Abs`` es la única función sin derivada: no es derivable en cero y no "
"existe un nodo ``sign`` con el que escribir su derivada, de modo que "
":meth:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Expression.diff` lanza un error sobre "
"ella."

#: ../../modules/core/core_terms_maps_comparisons.rst:178
msgid ""
"For powers, use the ``**`` operator, which builds a "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Pow` node and accepts a fractional or "
"symbolic exponent. :func:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Inv` is a shorthand "
"for ``x ** -1``, so ``Inv(x)``, ``1 / x`` and ``x ** -1`` are all the "
"same expression:"
msgstr ""
"Para las potencias, use el operador ``**``, que construye un nodo "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Pow` y admite un exponente fraccionario o "
"simbólico. :func:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Inv` es una abreviatura de ``x "
"** -1``, así que ``Inv(x)``, ``1 / x`` y ``x ** -1`` son todas la misma "
"expresión:"

#: ../../modules/core/core_terms_maps_comparisons.rst:202
msgid ""
"To write your own function, subclass "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Function` with a ``NAME``, a numeric "
"kernel and a derivative. Everything else (canonicalization, equality, "
"``diff``, ``expand``, ``substitute``, serialization) comes from the base "
"class."
msgstr ""
"Para escribir su propia función, cree una subclase de "
":class:`~qilisdk.core.expression.Function` con un ``NAME``, un núcleo "
"numérico y una derivada. Todo lo demás (canonización, igualdad, ``diff``,"
" ``expand``, ``substitute``, serialización) lo proporciona la clase base."

